  "step_3": "The decision reason requires consideration of the sum of all pairwise differences of outcomes. In this case, the pairwise differences are |6000 - 3000| = 3000 and |0 - 0| = 0, so the total sum is 3000 for both lotteries — meaning the sum of outcome differences is equal, and thus the reason would be indifferent. However, the individual does not mention this sum or any such calculation. Instead, the individual focuses on the prize size and probability, reasoning that B has a higher probability and thus is preferred. There is no mention of outcome differences or their sum. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason involving the sum of pairwise outcome differences. The justification is based on probability-weighted prize size, not on the sum of outcome differences. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
